        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> It would be cool if there was keymap to directly delete the buffer from the picker or at least show buffer id.\n\nThere is a [relatively concise example](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-pick.html#minipick.builtin.buffers) of how to achieve this.\n\nAll in all, I don't think simple visualization of buffer number adds much (at least compared to the code needed to achieve this robustly). It is usually more beneficial to create custom mappings to act on the buffer item directly inside the picker. Otherwise, indeed running `:buffers` is a good approach.\n\nClosing as not planned.",
